====================================================================================
 (B) REFRAME 1+2: change the observer / translate = GALILEAN invariance
====================================================================================
   base S=[1, 2, 5, 6, 7, 8], observer at 0: M=2/13
   observer copied onto runner w=1: relative speeds [0, 1, 4, 5, 6, 7] -> M=0  (changed)
   observer copied onto runner w=3: relative speeds [-2, -1, 2, 3, 4, 5] -> M=29/104  (changed)
   observer copied onto runner w=10: relative speeds [-9, -8, -5, -4, -3, -2] -> M=92/191  (changed)
   => moving the observer onto ANY runner = subtracting that speed = a GALILEAN shift; M is invariant.
      The danger-circulant lives on the GROUP Z/D, so it is translation-invariant by construction.

